DUT
**************************************************************************************************************************************
AXI4-Lite is a simple, memory-mapped, transaction-based protocol with decoupled address, data, and response channels.

Key properties (from ARM AMBA AXI spec):
Single-beat transfers only (no bursts)
Separate read and write paths
VALID / READY handshaking
Pipelined and decoupled

AXI4-Lite Handshake rule (core rule)
A transfer happens when VALID && READY on a rising clock edge.
And:
VALID must stay high until READY
Payload must stay stable while waiting
This single rule drives all FSMs.

AXI4-Lite ordering guarantees (important for bridge)
Only one outstanding transaction per channel
No IDs
Responses must be in order

👉 This makes AXI4-Lite bridge-friendly.
***************************************************************************************************************************************
APB is a simple, non-pipelined, synchronous peripheral bus with strict timing phases.

Key properties (from ARM APB spec):
One transfer at a time
No decoupling
Address, control, and data are phase-based
Optional wait states using PREADY

APB Transfer Phases (THIS is critical)
🔹 SETUP phase
PSEL = 1
PENABLE = 0
Address and control are driven

🔹 ACCESS phase
PSEL = 1
PENABLE = 1
Transfer completes when PREADY = 1
If PREADY = 0 → wait state.

| Operation | Signals                     |
| --------- | --------------------------- |
| Write     | `PWRITE=1`, `PWDATA` valid  |
| Read      | `PWRITE=0`, sample `PRDATA` |

***************************************************************************************************************************************

| Function             | Block                           |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| AXI request handling | `axi_write_fsm`, `axi_read_fsm` |
| Command packing      | FSM / `axi_cmd_pack`            |
| Decoupling           | `cmd_fifo`                      |
| Execution            | `apb_master_fsm`                |
| Translation          | `response_gen`                  |
| Integration          | `axi_apb_bridge_top`            |

****************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 axi_write_fsm
AXI rule it implements
AW and W are independent
Both must be accepted before response
BRESP sent only after completion

What this FSM does
Waits for AWVALID && AWREADY
Waits for WVALID && WREADY
Stores address + data
Emits ONE write command
Waits for completion
Drives BVALID/BRESP

This FSM does not care about APB timing
*******************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 axi_read_fsm
AXI rule it implements
AR accepted independently
R response must contain data + status
VALID/READY rules apply

What this FSM does
Accepts AR
Emits ONE read command
Waits for read data
Drives RVALID/RDATA/RRESP
*******************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 axi_cmd_pack (if used)
AXI rule it implements
AXI info arrives fragmented
Internal logic wants atomic commands

What it does
Combines AXI pieces into one command
This is an architectural convenience, not protocol requirement.
*******************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 cmd_fifo
Protocol problem it solves
AXI can issue requests faster
APB can only execute one at a time

What it does
Buffers commands
Preserves order
Applies backpressure
This is where decoupling is handled
*******************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 apb_master_fsm
APB rule it implements
SETUP → ACCESS → COMPLETE
Wait on PREADY
Sample PRDATA / PSLVERR

What this FSM does
Takes one command
Drives APB signals
Waits until done
Produces result

This FSM knows nothing about AXI
********************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 apb_addr_decoder
APB rule it implements
Multiple slaves selected by address

What it does
Decodes address
Generates one-hot PSELx
********************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 response_gen
Protocol rule it implements
AXI and APB signal errors differently

What it does
Maps PSLVERR → BRESP/RRESP
Passes PRDATA → RDATA
*********************************************************************************************************************************************
🔹 axi_apb_bridge_top
What it does (architectural role)
Connects everything
Does NOT implement protocol logic
Makes ownership explicit

Integration happens here, not in FSMs.
********************************************************************************************************************************************

The bridge exists to resolve this mismatch
| AXI4-Lite         | APB                 |
| ----------------- | ------------------- |
| Decoupled         | Strictly sequential |
| Pipelined         | Non-pipelined       |
| Multiple channels | Single channel      |
| Handshake-based   | Phase-based         |

